# Separate-compilation: stage 1 uses an older Scala compiler (Scala 2.13.x or
# Scala 3.0.x) that has no Python backend, so its compile produces no `.pyir`
# in the staging output dir. Stage 2 (current scala-py compiler) cannot
# resolve symbols declared in stage 1's `.scala` source — same shape as
# `i4947b` and `toplevel-implicits` already excluded. The `c2.13.12` /
# `c3.0.2` filename suffix is the Vulpix dir-test stage compiler version.
backwardsCompat-implicitParens              # separate-compilation-resolution (A_1_c3.0.2.scala compiles with Scala 3.0.2 which has no Python backend; Test_2.scala then fails to resolve Bar/Bat/Bax/Baz)
